                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1738: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-03T16:00:00-03:00">March 3, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. My 79, March 1, 3 p.m. Upon checking more closely Aranha says that under his
                    last offer dollar bondholders holding only 35.4% of the debt would receive 38.9%
                    of the payment to be made; the respective percentages for the others would be:
                    Sterling 60.8 and 58.4; francs 3.4 and 2.4; florins .4 and .3.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
